 it's more  reasoned why his party is widening the  gap  are you now calling on him to resign yes  he's lost the support from key democrats  in washington  and in his own backyard we are  considering  developing articles of impeachment of  governor cuomo  cuomo's lawyers intend to provide  evidence by next week  in his defense to stave off political  elimination but with a job approval  rating below 30 percent  cuomo's on borrowed time impeachment is  backed by a majority of state lawmakers  and as more investigations into his  behavior open up this is obviously a  very high profile investigation  there's a lot of information out there  his political future is on the line  with few people coming to his defense  democrats have been quick to cut ties  with scandal-plagued lawmakers in sharp  contrast to republicans who still stand  by a twice impeached former president  if cuomo can run through the headwinds  of his own impeachment it's unclear if  he could even seek a fourth term in 2022  given the lack of support and any  outcomes of current or former  investigations  jeff reggie takini in washington thanks  reggie  still ahead calls for accountability in  beirut  one year after the deadly port blast  you're watching global national  welcome back this week people in beirut  marked one year since that huge ammonium  nitrate explosion  killed 200 people causing devastating  damage in the lebanese capital  people there are angry that no senior  official has been held accountable  and they're also desperate for something  to be done about the country's deep  economic crisis and political  dysfunction redmond shannon reports  the new memorial for the beirut blast is  made from the debris of the explosion  many lebanese say for now justice for  the victims and political reform  are more important than sculptures the  killers  have complete impunity of their crime  and with already pretending that  something has passed on the anniversary  that frustration was visible on the  streets of beirut  and from french president emmanuel  macron who demanded fundamental change  as he chaired a lebanon aid conference  to help those  most in need i can tell you that  children for example now  replace staples such as cheese and egg  with only water and time and families  and parents tell me this  the economic crisis began a year before  the blast  medicines and fuel are scarce  electricity  intermittent we are looking at a crisis  where the very survival of children  is now at stake i'm sorry by the way i'm  sweating because  i have no electricity and it's 32  degrees here  economists say the collapse of the  currency is a result of decades of  mismanagement by lawmakers  so you import a lot but you are  subsidizing  and we as lebanese we were living above  our means you need a new mentality new  people who will  protect the public resources who will  manage the resources efficiently parties  have struggled to agree on a new  government  even amid the crisis this is partly  because the unique political system sees  key roles shared among religious groups  sectarian violence this week has  highlighted deep divides  that persist we used to talk about  failed states  you know we're past failed states you  know this is like  stateless uh somebody mentioned today  something like state capture  the political and social influence of  iran is seen by many  as the most insurmountable barrier to  change  some see only one solution for  themselves you know definitely anybody  who had another citizenship has already  left  because this is their password to live  hope  along with food and electricity remain  in  short supply in lebanon redmond shannon  global news  london she's been dubbed the fossil  fairy next meet the little girl who just  gave a big gift  to paleontologists in alberta  welcome back alberta is home to 587  animal species and for a long time that  list has not included  camels the desert dwellers haven't  roamed north america since the last ice  age  but newly unearthed evidence is now  shedding light on their prehistoric life  and as sarah ryan explains it's all  thanks to a six-year-old girl  six-year-old abby darby will never  forget this particular beach day  on the beach sand i thought i  saw a cool rock but then i digged it out  and it wasn't a rock instead of throwing  it back into jackfish lake  she ran to show her family the unusual  find  i thought after that it would be really  cool if i could tell her  exactly what it was because we all had  our guesses  grandma she had a clog  guest but all the other ones  um think that it was a tooth abby's aunt  sent a video of the fossil to the  university of alberta  it's definitely a tooth you can see it  right away and it's definitely mammal  because it has the multiple roots  a lot of what we see in dinosaurs or  lizards or other animals is a single  root  phd student mark powers looked carefully  at the tooth cusps and pits  upon looking at some specimens here at  the university of alberta in our  teaching collections i can confirm it's  definitely a camel  family member that's right a camel in  alberta  power says fossil records indicate  camels originated here in north america  abby was thrilled by the news i think  that  it was amazing the university estimates  the tooth to be between 22  and 25 000 years old there was huge  glaciers that were covering most of  alberta during that time so there would  have been  some ravines where the ice sheets were  retreating away from each other  where we would get a lot of water  influence from the militant glaciers and  that's where animals probably would have  hung out  power said by analyzing the fossilized  tooth isotopes  researchers could learn a lot about how  long the animal lived what it ate  and how it migrated abby's family plans  to donate the specimen to the royal  alberta museum  so when next year i'm in on grade one i  can show my friends  they would think it was very very cool  sarah ryan global news very cool  and that is global national for this  saturday night i'm jeff semple tonight  your canada is tiverton nova scotia  please keep sending us your photos to  viewers at globalnational.com  thanks for watching i'll see you back  here tomorrow have a great night
 

